<title>FINLAND: POLL- MARKKA LINK TO ERM SEEN AROUND 3.03 PER MARK.</title>
<headline>POLL- MARKKA LINK TO ERM SEEN AROUND 3.03 PER MARK.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Finnish markka is expected to be pegged to the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM) with a central parity rate around 3.03 per mark, according to a Reuters poll of 10 market operators covering Finland.</p>
<p>The average of the 10 DEM/FIM estimates in the poll conducted on Thursday was 3.025. The median, as well as the most frequent entry, was 3.03. Forecasts ranged between 3.00 and 3.052.</p>
<p>DEM/FIM on Thursday traded between 2.985 and 2.99 per mark in Helsinki.</p>
<p>The following banks and brokerages contributed to the poll:</p>
<p>Aktia Bank, Alfred Berg, Enskilda Helsinki, Evli Securities, Handelsbanken Finland, Merita Bank, OKOBANK, Postipankki, Selin Finance and Unibank Copenhagen.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
